---
/**
 * Three-step setup. Each card has a different motion accent — the cube,
 * theme picker, and pulsing launch ring are all pure CSS, no JS.
 */
---

<section class="how" id="how">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker">How it ships</div>
    <h2 class="sec-title" data-r>
      From zero, to <em>signed in</em>,<br />in three steps.
    </h2>
    <p class="sec-sub" data-r>
      Three commands, ten minutes. Nothing to deploy, nothing to pay for until you're past 5k MAU.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="how-grid">
    <div class="how-step" data-r>
      <div class="how-num">STEP 01</div>
      <h3>Tell us about <em>your app</em>.</h3>
      <p>
        Name, domain, providers you need. We provision a hosted portal, API keys, and a signed-releases
        SDK for your stack — automatically.
      </p>
      <div class="how-viz">
        <div class="viz-cube">
          <div class="c-wrap">
            <div class="f front"></div>
            <div class="f back"></div>
            <div class="f right"></div>
            <div class="f left"></div>
            <div class="f top"></div>
            <div class="f bot"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="how-step" data-r>
      <div class="how-num">STEP 02</div>
      <h3>Pick <em>your theme</em>.</h3>
      <p>
        Start from a preset, swap colors, upload a logo. Every hosted portal, every email, every error
        page — themed at once.
      </p>
      <div class="how-viz">
        <div class="viz-themes">
          <div class="t"></div>
          <div class="t active"></div>
          <div class="t"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="how-step" data-r>
      <div class="how-num">STEP 03</div>
      <h3>Edit &amp; <em>launch</em>.</h3>
      <p>
        Mount the handler, guard what matters. Policies by tenant, role, or domain. Every change
        audit-logged automatically.
      </p>
      <div class="how-viz">
        <div class="viz-launch">
          <div class="ring"></div>
          <div class="ring"></div>
          <div class="ring"></div>
          <div class="core">↑</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
